-- title:
--   Lemma 3.8 — Independent rounding
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a simple graph on $n$ labelled vertices and let $1\le T\le n$ be an integer. Let $z_1,\dots,z_T$ be integral orientation rules (for example those of Algorithm 1) and $\bar z=\frac1T\sum_t z_t$ their average fractional rule. For each pair $u<v$ choose an iteration $I(u,v)$ uniformly from $\{1,\dots,T\}$, independently over the pairs, and give the pair its direction in $z_{I(u,v)}$. Let $D$ be the orientation of $H$ induced by the resulting rule. Then
--
--   $$\Pr\Big[\|b_D-b_{\bar z}\|_1\le\frac{4n^2}{\sqrt T}\Big]\ge\frac12 .$$
--
--   This is the rounding step of the warm-up protocol: one random integral orientation whose imbalance stays close to that of the average.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The independent uniform choices are the uniform law on choice functions $I$ from the pairs $u<v$ to $\{1,\dots,T\}$, so the probability is the fraction of choice functions for which the bound holds.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - generalization: the rules $z_1,\dots,z_T$ generated by Algorithm 1 → every family of $T$ integral rules `z : Fin T → Rule n`; reason: the proof uses only that each $z_t$ is integral, $\deg_H\le n$ and $T\le n$; taking `z t := warmRule H b T t` gives the source's statement
--   - encoding: independent uniform choices $I_{uv}\in\{1,\dots,T\}$ → a uniform choice function `I : Pairs n → Fin T`, probability as a counting ratio (`roundingProb`); reason: the product of independent uniform laws is the uniform law on choice functions
--   - encoding: the sampled orientation $D$ and $b_{\bar z}$ → `induced H (roundRule z I)` and `fractionalImbalance H (avgRules z)`; reason: the same objects
-- source:
--   Henry Fleischmann, Sagnik Mukhopadhyay, Swagato Sanyal, STOC 2027 submission #503 (October 2026), p. 9, Lemma 3.8 (PDF p. 11); restated p. 15 (PDF p. 17), proof pp. 15–16 (PDF pp. 17–18)

import Definitions.Def_SubquadCutReach_Faster_Supplement_Warmup

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace SubquadCutReach.Faster.Supplement

open SubquadCutReach.Faster

/-- Lemma 3.8, p. 9 (PDF 11), restated p. 15 (PDF 17). Stated for every family of `T`
integral rules, in particular those of Algorithm 1. -/
theorem lemma_3_8 (n T : ℕ) (hT1 : 1 ≤ T) (hTn : T ≤ n) (H : SimpleGraph (Fin n))
    (z : Fin T → Rule n) :
    (1 : ℝ) / 2 ≤ roundingProb z fun D =>
      l1 (fun v => (imbalance (induced H D) v : ℝ) - fractionalImbalance H (avgRules z) v) ≤
        4 * (n : ℝ) ^ 2 / Real.sqrt (T : ℝ) := by sorry

end SubquadCutReach.Faster.Supplement
